{{Quote|That's why ''everyone'' gives in to a Bor. Not to make the pain stop. But so there's something ''left'' of you ''afterwards''.|An [[Unidentified Imperial interrogation officer|Imperial interrogation officer]]|<ref name="Aphra 22" />}}
'''Mairan''', also referred to as '''mind flayers''', or as '''Bors''', were a [[Sentience|sentient]] multi-[[Limb|tentacled]] multipod [[species]] that were [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Maires]]. They had the unique ability to read minds, and as a result, they were often used as a form of [[torture]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Partisans]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Bor Gullet can feel your thoughts. No lie is safe. ''[...]'' Bor Gullet will know the truth. The unfortunate side-effect is that one tends to lose one's mind.|Saw Gerrera, to [[Bodhi Rook]]|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:Mairan-Alien_Archive.jpg|thumb|250px|left|A Mairan]]
Mairan, sometimes known as Bors,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> were a [[Sentience|sentient]]<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion" /> multi-[[Limb|tentacled]] multipod [[species]] hailing from [[Maires]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> They were unique for being able to read minds and erase, or alter, memories.<ref name="Aphra 22" /> It was known for some individuals, such as the Imperial [[shuttle]] [[pilot]] Bodhi Rook, to lose their minds after having their mind plundered by a Mairan.<ref name="Rogue One" /> The [[Imperial Security Bureau]] conducted "[[Kadiopa experiment 9484-2]]"<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref> sometime before or during [[3 ABY]] <ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> where they used a bor to exude false intel provided by a plant from a group of prisoners. The ISB noted that several of the prisoners were left with permanent neurological damage.<ref name="Outlaws" />

==Mairans in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Why, for this very prisoner we are defrosting a bor of the Mairan&mdash;one of only three in Imperial hands.|An [[Unidentified prison warden|Imperial warden]], to [[Magna Tolvan]]|<ref name="Aphra 21">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 21|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 21]]</ref>}}
[[Saw Gerrera]]'s [[Partisans]] kept a Mairan named [[Bor Gullet]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[Galactic Empire]] kept three Mairans in [[Water|ice]], occasionally defrosting them to interrogate [[prisoner]]s,<ref name="Aphra 21" /> with [[Bor Ifriem]] being used to interrogate [[Chelli Lona Aphra|Chelli Aphra]] in [[Accresker Jail]].<ref name="Aphra 22" /> Decades later, [[Harra]] the [[Hutt]] kept a Mairan at [[Harra the Hutt's stronghold|her stronghold]] on [[Vodran]]. At one point it was used on [[Cost Niktur]].<ref name="Escape from Vodran">''[[Join the Resistance: Escape from Vodran]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Mairan first appeared in the [[Gareth Edwards]]' [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Although the [[canon]] novel ''[[Join the Resistance: Escape from Vodran]]'', written by [[Ben Acker]] and [[Ben Blacker]], identified them as Bors,<ref name="Escape from Vodran" /> [[Doctor Aphra (2016) 21|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 21]], a canon [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] written by [[Simon Spurrier]] and penciled by [[Kev Walker]], identified the Mairans for the first time.<ref name="Aphra 21" /> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' legends]], the Mairan first appeared in the novel ''[[Young Jedi Knights: Lightsabers]]'', written by [[Kevin J. Anderson]] and [[Rebecca Moesta]].<ref name="Young Jedi Knights">''[[Young Jedi Knights: Lightsabers]]''</ref>

